Appendix A – 200+ Word Report Description for Submission

This report presents a detailed analysis of the current cybersecurity threat landscape, with emphasis on recent developments reported during 2025 and 2026. The study examines major cyber threats affecting organizations, including ransomware, phishing and social engineering, vulnerability exploitation, credential theft, malware and infostealers, supply-chain compromise, cloud security risks, DDoS attacks, insider threats and AI-enabled attacks. The report identifies common attack vectors and explains how threat actors can combine multiple techniques to move from initial access to privilege escalation, lateral movement, data theft and operational impact. It also analyzes the possible consequences of cyber incidents across confidentiality, integrity and availability, along with financial, operational, legal and reputational effects. Recent findings from trusted sources such as ENISA, Verizon, Microsoft and Google Cloud/Mandiant are used to support the analysis and to distinguish current evidence from general cybersecurity observations. Special attention is given to the growing role of artificial intelligence in accelerating reconnaissance, phishing, vulnerability discovery, malware development and attack automation. The report concludes with practical recommendations covering identity security, vulnerability management, ransomware resilience, email security, supply-chain risk, cloud security, AI governance, incident response and disaster recovery. The overall objective is to provide a structured and evidence-based understanding of how modern cyber threats can affect organizations and how layered security controls can reduce exposure, improve detection, limit damage and strengthen organizational cyber resilience.

